* THE UMBILICAL, every conductor: 2 m of Cat5e (Belden 1752A, banked) as eight coupled
* conductors in four twisted pairs, pinned as umbilical-pinmap: 1/2 BREATH/AGND_SENSE,
* 3/6 +12V/PWR_GND, 4/5 SCLK/MOSI, 7/8 CS/DIG_GND. GENERATED by a script from the
* per-metre matrices sims.yaml derives (cl_*); every value is filled from sims.yaml.
* The matrices are those of a PERFECTLY TWISTED cable: in-pair loop inductance
* z_diff / v (spi-link/sim's odd mode, from the datasheet), pair-to-pair loop z_cm / v
* (spi-link/sim's even mode, swept there), and C = L^-1 / v^2 (a homogeneous dielectric
* at the datasheet's velocity). The reference is a fictitious remote conductor, left
* floating: the instrument is isolated, so the sum of the eight currents is zero, and the
* total mode's inductance (cl_lp) carries nothing. Perfect twist decouples every pair's
* differential mode from every other; the twist's imbalance is added as the datasheet's
* maximum capacitance unbalance (c_unb), lumped half at each end, from BREATH to the
* aggressor conductor each sim names (k_unb_pwr: +12V; k_unb_spi: SCLK).
*
* UMB_LUMPED: two pi-sections, for the runs that last milliseconds (ngspice's CPL steps at
* the line's own delay, ~10 ns, which no millisecond run can afford).
* UMB_CPL: the same matrices as ngspice CPL; sim cable-check holds the lumped form to it.
.subckt UMB_LUMPED m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 i1 i2 i3 i4 i5 i6 i7 i8
